  <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">StackGeist</a> / <a href="/gear">Gear</a> / <a href="/gear/budget-tech">Budget tech</a> / Sennheiser Momentum 4</p>
  <p class="page-kicker">Worth paying more for · Audio</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Sennheiser Momentum 4 Wireless Noise-Cancelling Headphones</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">60-hour battery, class-leading audio in the sub-Sony-XM5 tier, credible ANC. The correct answer if audio quality matters as much as noise cancellation.</p>
  <img class="hero" src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71BjWi3lbCL._AC_SL1500_.jpg" alt="Sennheiser Momentum 4 Wireless Noise-Cancelling Headphones" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" style="display:block;width:100%;max-height:420px;object-fit:contain;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;margin:24px 0" />

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">Quick verdict</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">The tier below Sony XM5 / Bose 700 where value peaks.</h2>
    <p>Sennheiser's Momentum 4 Wireless is the correct answer if you want premium-tier audio quality with credible noise cancellation and 60-hour battery in a package that doesn't cost as much as the Sony XM5 / Bose Ultra flagships. The ANC is a hair behind Sony's; the audio is noticeably better than Sony's if you actually listen to music. Multipoint pairing, aptX Adaptive, USB-C. The right buy for anyone whose primary use is listening to music with ANC as a secondary benefit — not the other way around.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">The problem it solves</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Noise makes focus impossible.</h2>
    <p>Open offices, coffee shops, apartments with thin walls, trains, and planes all share the same problem: ambient noise that pulls focus away from work and makes calls harder to hear. Passive isolation (over-ear cushions blocking sound) handles maybe 20 dB of it. Active noise cancellation adds another 20-30 dB in the low-frequency range where most annoying noise lives (HVAC hum, engine drone, distant traffic).</p><p>The Momentum 4's ANC is not the class-leading Sony or Bose implementation, but it's within a few dB, and the difference is only audible in direct A/B testing. For daily use, the ANC is more than enough to make an open office bearable.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">Verified specs</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">What Sennheiser lists.</h2>
    <ul><li>42mm dynamic drivers</li><li>Adaptive Noise Cancellation with transparency mode</li><li>Up to 60 hours battery per charge with ANC on</li><li>USB-C fast charging (10 minutes = 6 hours playback)</li><li>Bluetooth 5.2 with multipoint (two devices at once)</li><li>aptX Adaptive, aptX, AAC, SBC codec support</li><li>4 mic beamforming array for calls</li><li>Weight: 293g</li><li>Sennheiser Smart Control app for EQ and firmware</li></ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">Compatibility check</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Where it works well, where it doesn't.</h2>
    <p><strong>Works well with:</strong> iPhone (AAC), Android (aptX Adaptive if the phone supports it), macOS (AAC), Windows (aptX or AAC with the right driver), Linux (Bluetooth stack limitations may cap you at SBC).</p><p><strong>Multipoint pairing:</strong> Two devices simultaneously. Swap audio between laptop and phone without unpairing. Works reliably across firmware updates.</p><p><strong>3.5mm wired mode:</strong> Included cable. Works even when battery is dead. USB-C wired audio: does not work — the USB-C port is charge-only.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">Real-world use cases</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Where 60-hour battery earns its keep.</h2>
    <p><strong>Full work-from-home week.</strong> Charge Sunday night, use for 8-hour workdays through Friday without recharging. Fewer chargers, fewer dead-headphone moments mid-call.</p><p><strong>Long-haul flights.</strong> Coast-to-coast, transatlantic, transpacific — one charge covers the whole trip. Sony XM5 is close but not equal here.</p><p><strong>Open office / shared workspace.</strong> ANC on, put them on when you need to focus. Transparency mode for quick conversations without pulling them off.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">Tradeoffs and deal-breakers</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Where they lose to alternatives.</h2>
    <ul><li><strong>ANC is not class-leading.</strong> Sony XM5 and Bose Ultra edge them out in raw noise reduction. If ANC is your #1 priority, buy those instead.</li><li><strong>Call microphone quality is average.</strong> Adequate for calls but nothing to praise. AirPods Max is better at this specifically.</li><li><strong>App is decent, not great.</strong> Basic EQ, adaptive noise cancellation controls, firmware update. No spatial audio features on the app side.</li><li><strong>Case is bulky.</strong> Larger than Sony XM5 case. Fits in a backpack but not a jacket pocket.</li><li><strong>Fit is snug for very small heads.</strong> Try before buying if you have a smaller frame.</li></ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">Better alternatives</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">When to buy something else.</h2>
    <p><strong>Sony WH-1000XM5.</strong> ~$350. Better ANC by a small margin, worse audio quality for critical listening, better call mic. Buy this if ANC beats audio quality for your use.</p><p><strong>Anker Soundcore Q30.</strong> ~$70. Sub-$100 ANC option with credible noise reduction and 40-hour battery. Not close to Momentum 4 on audio quality but 5x cheaper. Compared these directly here: <a href="/gear/budget-tech/compare/sennheiser-momentum-4-vs-cheap-anc">Momentum 4 vs Soundcore Q30</a>.</p><p><strong>Apple AirPods Max.</strong> ~$500. Best-in-class if you're all-in on Apple. Overkill and overpriced for anyone else. Physical build is heavier than Momentum 4.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading"></h2>
    <div class="cards"><div class="card"><h3>Are they comfortable for 8-hour days?</h3><p>Yes for most head shapes. Lighter than Bose 700, similar to Sony XM5. Cushions are memory foam and don't cause hot spots.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Do they support LDAC or aptX Lossless?</h3><p>aptX Adaptive yes. LDAC no. aptX Lossless requires Snapdragon Sound-certified phones, which the Momentum 4 supports on paper but real-world availability is limited.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>How is call quality on Zoom / Teams?</h3><p>Adequate. Not the reason to buy them. AirPods and Bose 700 both have better call mics.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Can I use them wired if the battery dies?</h3><p>Yes. Included 3.5mm cable. USB-C is charge-only for audio.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>60 hours realistic or marketing?</h3><p>Realistic. Sennheiser under-promises here — with ANC on at moderate volume, real-world use is 55-65 hours.</p></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">Buy or skip</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading"></h2>
    <div class="cards"><div class="card"><h3>Buy this if</h3><p>You want premium-tier ANC headphones where audio quality matters as much as noise cancellation, and 60-hour battery is a real advantage for your travel or work rhythm.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Skip this if</h3><p>ANC is your only priority (Sony XM5), you want the best call mic (AirPods Max), or you need a sub-$100 option (Soundcore Q30).</p></div></div>
  </section>

